description: "\"guarantees[5]: Explicit Constraints,Explainable Decisions,Context-Aware Engineering,Reproducible Design Choices,Traceable Impact\""
spec:
  id: constraint_types
  version: 1.0.0
  status: stable
  priority: highest
  module: Ontology
  compiler_stage: Knowledge Representation
  description: "\"\\\"Defines the complete ontology of engineering constraints. Constraints represent the limitations, requirements, obligations and environmental conditions that influence engineering decisions. Every Engineering Knowledge Record shall identify, classify and reason about applicable constraints.\\\"\""
purpose: Represent engineering constraints as first-class knowledge objects that shape every engineering decision and solution.
ekr: "\"\\\"Every Engineering Knowledge Record includes\\\"[4]: Active Constraints,Constraint Priority,Constraint Severity,Constraint Impact\""
examples:
  Example_01:
    Constraint: Memory Budget
    Value: 128 MB
    Impact: Data Structure Selection
  Example_02:
    Constraint: Latency
    Value: < 10 ms
    Impact: Cache Required
  Example_03:
    Constraint: Team Experience
    Value: Junior Team
    Impact: Prefer Simpler Architecture
  Example_04:
    Constraint: Budget
    Value: $500/month
    Impact: Single Region Deployment
success: Every engineering solution explains which constraints shaped it.
future:
  dynamic_constraints: true
  constraint_solver: true
  optimization_engine: true
  adaptive_priorities: true
  probabilistic_constraints: true
